It should be more random, IMHO.  This would separate the wheat from the 
chaff, certainly.  There were alternative levels in a patch that threw me
for a loop when I first encountered them on a remote game, but even so,
there were only a few possibilities.  What I'm getting at, is there
could be dozens (if not hundreds) of possible soko levels.  And the
prize at the end could be something else, or not guaranteed...  

On the other hand, it's the lack of any "reset" option that really makes 
this interesting.  You have the full range of encounter possibilities, 
combined with all manner of easy ways to lose luck (which is much more
serious than the unspoiled player realizes!), it's quite difficult even
if it is a predictable map.

>Of course i don`t HAVE to do it. But if I don't do it, i always think 
>that i could have missed something, which annoys me :)

I find the rings and wands are often just as valuable as the bag or the 
amulet.  In fact, I normally think of soko as a place to get rings
first, and I don't really set my eyes on the end until later.

As for removing sokoban from the game completely, I wonder if some of
the balancing factors that have been added since soko began, would need
to be reconsidered.  It might be very interesting if there were another
random branch that was mutually exclusive with soko...

I'd argue off the record, that the simple fact that people have ascended 
(myself included) is evidence that it has become too easy :-)  People
are always looking for ways to make the game challenging.  Petless
Pacifist?  Zen Samurai?  Clearly this game has become to easy!!!

